 "unit": "EUR bn at the customs layer (the layer of trade_full.json, narrow.json trade_layer and refresh_2026.json), converted at trade_full.json fx; national figures also given in million USD as published",
 "question": "Do the Eurasian Economic Commission's mutual-trade statistics and the EAEU members' national statistics give a second, independent measurement of trade with Russia (to_rus = imports from Russia, from_rus = exports to Russia) for KAZ, KGZ, ARM and BLR, and do they change ranges, letters or centrals?",
 "answer_short": {
  "eec_after_2021": "No pair data. Every EEC mutual-trade product (tables, time series, express information, analytical reviews, bulletins, annual report on mutual trade) ends at January 2022 or 2021; checked 2026-10-25. The EEC socio-economic briefs for 2022-2025 contain no trade at all, and the payments express (2025) gives currency shares only and notes that the Bank of Russia has suspended its data. The EEC publishes no Russia-reported flows after 2021.",
  "independence": "Not independent. The national figures (BNS Kazakhstan, NSC Kyrgyzstan, Armstat) are the reporters' own statistics, the same records they send to UN Comtrade and the IMF; they match Comtrade to 0.0-0.4% wherever both carry the final vintage. Same source family 'trade'. The only independent measurement, Russia's own report, stops in 2021 (Comtrade r643 and the EEC 2015-2021 pair tables carry the same Russian figures).",
  "letter": "No change. A part needs two official families for A; these add none.",
  "ranges": "Kazakhstan: nothing new except an exact 2026 figure (already used to 0.1%). Armenia: 2026 January-August moves from press-based to Armstat's official chapter (central +5.8% imports, +2.2% exports; band about +-3% instead of +-8%). Kyrgyzstan: no narrowing; the site's 2024, 2025 and 2026 values sit below the National Statistical Committee's current figures by 18-30% (imports) and 18-50% (exports), outside the site's high bound.",
  "centrals": "Kyrgyzstan to_rus rises by about EUR 1.15bn over 2022-2026 at the customs layer after the 2019-2021 base moves up (about 8% of one year's GDP, toward Russia). Kyrgyzstan from_rus: reported exports +0.39 (base included), residual -0.52 (2024, 2025 and 2026 at 8/12 of 2025), net about -0.13 (about -1% of GDP); mostly a shift from estimate to report. Armenia +0.09 to_rus, -0.04 from_rus (under 0.5% of GDP) and Kazakhstan 0.00: both stay near zero. Belarus: nothing new after 2021."
 },
